- Status is declared, never inferred,[1Cfor[1Crunners[1Cthat[1Ctalk.[20;3H-[1CStorage[1Cfailure[1Cis[1Ca[1Chalt,[1Cnot[1Ca[1Cdegraded[1Cmode.[21;3H-[1CObserved[1Cdata[1Cnever[1Coverwrites[1Can[1Coverride.[22;3H-[1CA[1Ccard[1Ccannot[1Cbe[1Cmoved[1Cout[1Cof[1Ca[1Cwaiting[1Cstate[1Cwithout[1Canswering[1Cwhat[1Cit[1Cholds.[24;3HMy[1Cconcerns[1Cfall[1Cinto[1Cfour[1Cgroups:[26;3H-[1CThe[1Cdocument[1Cis[1Cstale[1Cin[1Cplaces,[1Cand[1Cseveral[1Cstatements[1Cnow[1Ccontradict[1Ceach[1Cother.[27;3H-[1CThe[1Cschema[1Cin[1Cthe[1Cdoc[1Chas[1Cdrifted[1Cfrom[1Cwhat[1Cthe[1Cprose[1Cdescribes.[28;3H-[1CThe[1Cremote-access[1Cstory[1Cleaves[1Cthe[1Chuman-facing[1CAPI[1Cwith[1Ca[1Cvery[1Clarge[1Cblast[1Cradius.[29;3H-[1CA[1Cfew[1Crules[1Cinteract[1Cin[1Cways[1Cthe[1Cdocument[1Cdoes[1Cnot[1Cexamine.

  I read only this file. I did not check any claim against the code, so "the doc says X" does not mean "the code does   
  X."[115C
[120C
  [1mWhat[22m [1mthe[22m [1mdesign[22m [1mgets[22m [1mright[22m[K[92C
[120C
  [1mTask[22m [1mas[22m [1mthe[22m [1mnoun[22m[K[102C
[120C
  Moving from "an agent that POSTed" to a durable task fixes the real problem. Identity survives restarts, and history  
  attaches to intent instead of to a pid. The reasoning in "Identity and registration" is sound:[24C
[120C
  - Pids are recycled, so pid-as-identity splits or merges cards.[55C
  - Demoting pid to a matching hint (same pid, same worktree, still alive) is the right level of trust.[17C
  - Two registration paths cover launched and self-started runners without a handshake.[33C
  - The daemon asks the model for [38;2;177;185;249mwhy [monce, because intent is the one fact the code cannot know.[K[24C
[120C
  [1mObserved[22m [1mversus[22m [1moverrides[22m[K[93C
[120C
  One JSON column and one resolution rule ("override if present, else observed") is cheap and easy to reason about. It  
  generalizes [38;2;177;185;249m/rename [minstead of adding a second copy of each field. The failure it prevents is real and easy to        
  describe: the operator names a card, the runner dies and reconnects, and the name survives.[27C
[120C
  [1mThe[22m [1mhalt[22m[K[110C
[120C
  This is the strongest section. Three tiers (refuse to start, retry contention, halt on anything else) leave no        
  partial-service state to test. Closing the listener converts a novel failure into connection refused, which the client
  already handles. The reasoning "a 500 would route through a path nothing has ever tested" is exactly right. The two   
  follow-ups it names (5xx treated as unreachable in the hook, and dedup keys) are the correct consequences.[12C
[120C
  [1mCapture[22m [1mversus[22m [1minterpret[22m[K[94C
[120C
  "Never infer status for a runner that talks" removes any need for a precedence table. Because non-cooperative runners 
  emit no competing signal, there is nothing to arbitrate. This is the kind of rule that stays true as the system grows.
[120C
  [1mFree[22m [1mquestions[22m [1mstay[22m [1mfree[22m[K[94C
[120C
  Goal 8 (answer everything that does not need a model) shows up in concrete mechanisms: liveness by syscall, standing  
  rules, diffs rendered from data, and hook-based registration. It is a good design principle, and the doc applies it   
  consistently.[105C
[120C
  [1mContradictions[22m [1mand[22m [1mstale[22m [1mcontent[22m[K[86C
[120C
  The document is partly a design and partly a changelog, and the seams show.[43C
[120C
